// Renovate preset for a repo that runs the security hotfix lane: a vulnerable
// dependency can be patched straight on the release branch (`main`) without
// waiting for everything on the integration branch (`develop`) to be ready.
//
// Use it IN ADDITION to the shared default, from the repo's own config:
//   {
//     extends: ["github>dodi-smart/.github", "github>dodi-smart/.github:security-hotfix"],
//     baseBranchPatterns: ["develop", "main"],
//   }
//
// The extending repo must set `baseBranchPatterns` itself. A repo's own setting
// wins over any preset, and the shared default pins `["develop"]`, so a preset
// cannot add `main` to it: without the repo's line, Renovate never looks at
// `main` and this file does nothing.
//
// What it does:
//   - A vulnerability alert is a `fix`, so its PR is titled `fix(deps): ...
//     [SECURITY]` and cuts a patch release. The shared default types every other
//     update `chore`.
//   - `main` gets those security PRs and nothing else. Without the first rule below,
//     Renovate would open every routine bump twice, once per base branch.
//
// What it needs:
//   - Dependabot alerts enabled on the repo. Renovate reads the vulnerabilities
//     of the repo from them; with alerts off there are none to patch.
//   - The `security_hotfix` repository property set to `enabled`. This file
//     does not read it: the PR Checks target guard does, and rejects a security
//     PR into `main` otherwise.
//
// A security PR into `main` is not merged by the dependency policy, which only
// merges into the default branch. The automerge workflow's `hotfix` job merges
// it once the lane verdict, PR Checks and an approving review agree, unless the
// HOTFIX_AUTOMERGE org variable is `false`; otherwise a person merges it.
//
// The filename is load-bearing. `github>owner/repo:security-hotfix` fetches
// `security-hotfix.json` from the repo root, by exactly that name. Comments are
// fine: Renovate parses a `.json` preset as JSONC.
{
  "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",

  "vulnerabilityAlerts": {
    "enabled": true,
    "semanticCommitType": "fix"
  },

  "packageRules": [
    {
      "description": "main receives security updates only. A vulnerability alert is added to the rules after these, without a base branch, so it still applies on main and switches updates back on there for the vulnerable package",
      "matchBaseBranches": ["main"],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "description": "A lock file refresh is not a security fix, and would otherwise be the one update type to slip onto main",
      "matchBaseBranches": ["main"],
      "matchUpdateTypes": ["lockFileMaintenance"],
      "enabled": false
    }
  ]
}
